    <string name="sample_question">What is the derivative of f(x) = 3x² + 2x - 5?</string>
    <string name="sample_answer">f\'(x) = 6x + 2</string>
    <string name="sample_explanation_visible">To find the derivative, we apply the power rule to each term:\n\n• For 3x²: bring down the exponent and reduce by 1\n  → 3 × 2x^(2-1) = 6x</string>
    <string name="sample_explanation_locked">• For 2x: the derivative of x is 1\n  → 2 × 1 = 2\n\n• For -5: the derivative of a constant is 0\n\nTherefore, f\'(x) = 6x + 2\n\nThis is a fundamental concept in calculus known as differentiation.</string>

